Whereabouts is GPL-3.0-or-later (see LICENSE). It is a fork of FindMyDevice.

The built-in push distributor, in app/src/main/java/com/wanderwildwood/ibasho/push/,
is adapted from two Apache-2.0 projects, whose licence is in LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt:

- Sunup, https://codeberg.org/Sunup/android, commit fe768d0 (1.3.3).
  The autopush WebSocket client and its message formats (api/ServerConnection.kt,
  api/MessageSender.kt, api/data/ClientMessage.kt, api/data/ServerMessage.kt) and the
  restart worker (services/RestartWorker.kt). Rewritten for Gson in place of
  kotlinx.serialization, reduced to one registration, and wired to the UnifiedPush
  connector inside this app rather than to other apps.

- UnifiedPush android-distributor, https://codeberg.org/UnifiedPush/android-distributor,
  commit 6daaf14 (0.7.6). The reconnection delays (SourceManager.getTimeout) and the
  approach of the foreground service and network callback.

Each file taken from them says so at the top. The changes are this project's, under
GPL-3.0-or-later.
